{"step_index":1615,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-25T23:19:14Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-25T18:19:14-05:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-25T18:19:19-05:00\nCreated At: 2026-11-25T18:19:14-05:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-25T18:19:19-05:00\nCommand exited with code 0.\n\nCommand output:\nTEXT 024e0e25: 'So bad news. The Ganado ended up getting totaled.'\r\nTEXT 03f726c6: 'Call Joey from your ~b~Contacts ~BLIP_APP_CONTACTS~~b~ or check the engine to tow and repair your vehicle.'\r\nTEXT 10356152: \"Working for Brian will require some gear from Ammu-Nation. Pick up a longarm at Chuck's Tackle & Shot.\"\r\nTEXT 1174eee2: \"A large-mouthed fish with silver-green scales, the Atlantic tarpon is found everywhere in Leonida's oceans, in both coastal and deeper waters.\"\r\nTEXT 11a59fbe: 'Liberty, Gellhorn, Alderney and Carcer had parachuted down into occupied Europe — either France or an even meeker country — and were immediately captured. They had escaped, killed over 5000 Arschlochkommandos in the process, before getting captured again. This time their prison camp had a fence, which made escape much harder.~n~~n~The Germans had rightfully identified Gellhorn as the main troublemaker, and put him in isolation, hoping to break his spirit. The mad Leonidan, however, soon turned the tables on his captors. Day in and day out, the guards outside his cell were driven mad by the unremitting sound of Gellhorn\\'s frenzied pumping, pausing only now and again for a breathless rendition of \"The Star-Spangled Banner\". When the last prison camp guard had finally succumbed — shrieking \"Nein!\" and shooting himself — Liberty had smartly identified his golden opportunity, commandeering their Übermacht motorbike and making an all-American jump straight through the fence. Loading up on guns, ammunition, explosives, cigars and Bratwurst, they were ready for phase three of the plan.~n~~n~Then there had been the hard and bloody tank battle at Panzerschlong. The surprisingly straightforward bombing of the dam at Wimpfken-Shmimpfken. The humbling moment of near defeat before the triumphant comeback at the compound in Klimaxburg.~n~~n~And then, the pièce de résistance: the final stage of their grand plan to win the war. At its heart, it was deceptively simple: the highest-ranking members of Germany\\'s political and military spheres were to be summoned to a remote château in the hills to attend a lavish dinner party hosted in celebration of the Führer himself. Except the Führer wouldn\\'t be there. Instead, those Krauts would be met by Captain Liberty, his squad, and enough dynamite to blow the Reich to hell and back and then back into hell again.~n~~n~By this point, Liberty\\'s life had almost finished flashing before his eyes. He caught final, fleeting glimpses of buxom French milkmaids with pails of cream, busty German waitresses'\r\nTEXT 25c45e20: \"The Ganado has seen better days. Get it fixed up and a new coat of paint at Joey's mod shop before Lucia's release.\"\r\nTEXT 4eafe833: \"She thrashed through the water with the speed of a Machairodontinae, climbing onto the land and gripping her weapon as she sprinted toward her prey, which was now on the move with the precision of a Muscardinus avellanarius.~n~~n~She whipped past tree branches, the sharp sting of the bark reminding her that she was alive. For the first time in ice ages, she smiled. She was gaining on her prize, and she could already hear her father's celebratory words. 'Booga ooga unga ooga', she'd hear him say, welcoming her home. As Nathalia leapt up and clicked her heels together in anticipation, she lost her footing.~n~~n~Her legs sprawled out underneath her, sending her flying down the forested hill and toward the edge of a cliff, crashing into trees as she desperately tried to slow herself down. The edge was near, and there was nothing to grab onto. As Nathalia closed her eyes and prayed for a quick end, something, or someone, grabbed her by the arm and pulled her to safety.~n~~n~Nathalia caught her breath and looked up at her savior. To her surprise, she saw those same brown eyes she had been chasing moments before. She lurched forward, pinning the animal down. What she saw was no Mammuthus primigenius, nor was it an Ursus\"\r\nTEXT 6793906b: 'Ammu-Nations ~BLIP_STYLE_STORE_GUN~ will offer weapon mods to improve its stats and performance.~n~~n~Attachments include custom grips ~BLIP_WEAPON_MOD_GRIP_ON~ magazines ~BLIP_WEAPON_MOD_MAG_ON~ optics ~BLIP_WEAPON_MOD_SIGHT_ON~ and more. Suppressors and tactical flashlights can be equipped and removed in your loadout. Other attachments can only be managed at an Ammu-Nation.~n~~n~Hold ~INPUT_OPEN_WHEEL_MENU~ to check your weapon stats and attached mods anytime in your loadout.~n~~n~~b~Tip:~b~ Hold ~INPUT_OPEN_WHEEL_MENU~ with a weapon equipped to quickly compare stats with a found weapon on the ground.'\r\nTEXT 68c88f67: \"A slim, silvery fish that can be identified by the yellow spots that decorate its scales, the mackerel can be found throughout Leonida's coastal waters.\"\r\nTEXT 7f2e2b17: 'The goliath grouper is a large saltwater fish with mottled, brownish scales, and favors tropical coastal waters and reefs.'\r\nTEXT 81415fda: \"If your vehicle takes enough damage, it will be destroyed and undrivable.~n~~n~If this happens to your personal vehicle it can be recovered. Unowned vehicles can't be recovered and are permanently destroyed.~n~~n~You can call Joey from your Contacts ~BLIP_APP_CONTACTS~ to have your vehicle repaired or delivered.~n~~n~~b~Tip:~b~ If your vehicle lands on its side or roof, approach it and hold ~INPUT_SHOVE~ to try and shove it back onto its wheels.\"\r\nTEXT 966f93d2: 'Jason heads to his local Ammu-Nation to pick up a longarm gun.'\r\nTEXT 97553638: 'Get your vehicle towed for repairs by calling Joey from your ~b~Contacts ~BLIP_APP_CONTACTS~~b~'\r\nTEXT 97d1139a: 'Leave the water and recover your vehicle by calling Joey.'\r\nTEXT 9a62eb65: 'Ammu-Nations ~BLIP_STYLE_STORE_GUN~ will offer weapon mods to improve its stats and performance.~n~~n~Attachments include custom grips ~BLIP_WEAPON_MOD_GRIP_ON~ magazines ~BLIP_WEAPON_MOD_MAG_ON~ optics ~BLIP_WEAPON_MOD_SIGHT_ON~ and more. Suppressors and tactical flashlights can be equipped and removed in your loadout. Other attachments can only be managed at an Ammu-Nation.~n~~n~Hold and release ~INPUT_OPEN_WHEEL_MENU~ to check your weapon stats and attached mods anytime in your loadout.~n~~n~~b~Tip:~b~ Hold and release ~INPUT_OPEN_WHEEL_MENU~ with a weapon equipped to quickly compare stats with a found weapon on the ground.'\r\nTEXT 9acb1db5: \"Bad news. The Ganado was totaled in the fire. Joey took it for scrap. It's still hot down here so keep laying low. You guys alright?\"\r\nTEXT 9cf5fd05: 'Distinguishable from the better-known American herring gull by its black head and distinctive call, the laughing gull can be seen in coastal regions and urban centers.'\r\nTEXT bd592f94: 'Found in coastal regions, forests, and wetlands, the corn snake can be recognized by its reddish scales. It kills by constriction, but is too small to pose a threat to humans. A gentle kill will preserve the quality of the carcass.'\r\nTEXT c1cf23c9: \"Hey this is Joey from Coastal Auto Care. Cal mentioned your car might need some work, let me know. Here's my spot.\"\r\nTEXT c8895c73: 'Cal has left a surprise for Jason with Joey. Speak with him at his garage in Key Lento.'\r\nTEXT d2d08f7e: \"I remember you telling me you used to drive a Phoenix right? I hope so cause... fuck it just go to Joey's and collect your surprise. ~BLIP_EMOJI_DEVIL_RED~\"\r\nTEXT d96f2817: 'Known for its singular call, the whooping crane is a tall, white wading bird with black-tipped wings and a red splash on its forehead. It can be found in wetlands and northern coastal regions.'\r\nTEXT e1f6fbf3: \"You're out of gas. Call Joey from your ~b~Contacts~b~ ~BLIP_APP_CONTACTS~ to request a tow and fuel up your vehicle.\"\r\nTEXT e4d917af: \"Hey this is Joey from Coastal Auto Care. Cal mentioned your car might need some work, let me know. Here's my spot.\"\r\nTEXT eb7f2e8f: 'BENOIT SUCRE — LOS SANTOS\\' AWARD-WINNING PASTRY CHEF — ON HIS FAVORITE RIFLE~n~~n~In my profession, we have a saying: presentation is everything. And that is true even of something as beautiful as the Kozlov KZ-59.~n~~n~Mine has a recipe of modifications for comfort and tactical advantage. 12\" barrel, modern stock, ergonomic grips, large aperture holo sight and a beautiful custom finish. All available at any good Ammu-Nation today!'\r\nTEXT ec1bc5b6: '~b~Tip:~b~ Call Joey from your ~b~Contacts~b~ ~BLIP_APP_CONTACTS~ to have your vehicle repaired or delivered.'\r\nTEXT f7aead1d: \"~BLIP_APP_AI_ASSISTANT~ Generated by WAiNK~n~~n~These columns protruding out of the sea appear to be part of a coral farm just off of Abismo Key. While sometimes used for scientific research and coastal reef restoration, they mainly supply the lucrative black-market trade of protected coral for dentist waiting rooms across Leonida. Corals are sentient marine invertebrates that form colonies of thousands of genetically identical 'polyps' which communicate with each other, share resources and collaborate efficiently on projects—an interesting organic precursor to agentic swarm intelligence.\"\r\nMD gta6_mission_flow_chart.md: size=35528 sha256=9bd9f01ca65c\r\nMD output\\antigravity_version\\gta6_mission_flow_chart.md: size=35528 sha256=9bd9f01ca65c\r\nMD C:\\Users\\<user>\\Downloads\\gta6_mission_flow_chart.md: size=35528 sha256=9bd9f01ca65c\r\nMD C:\\Users\\<user>\\Downloads\\antigravity_version\\gta6_mission_flow_chart.md: size=35528 sha256=9bd9f01ca65c\r\nMD C:\\Users\\<user>\\.gemini\\antigravity-cli\\brain\\96252013-4633-45e8-b6a2-59b18be9e68c\\gta6_mission_flow_chart.md: size=35528 sha256=9bd9f01ca65c\r\n"}
