|\n392: | **Ch. 3** | **51–52. Tyrone Strand** | `TYR_INTRO` | Dual Switching | 50. Real Estate | Street muscle contracts | Interleave with Boobie & Raul to avoid cooldowns |\n393: | **Ch. 3** | **54–56. Boobie Strand** | `CLB_INTRO` | Dual Switching | 50. Real Estate | Nightclub and Port of Vice City introductions | High syndicate reputation unlocked |\n394: | **Ch. 3** | **53, 57–60. Raul Strand**| `CAR_INTRO` | Dual Switching | 50. Real Estate | Cartel logistics and exotic car booster contracts | Unlocks Zorrusso supercar getaway vehicle |\n395: | **Ch. 3** | **61. Sinfrontera Scope Out**| `ROB_PREP_SCOP` | Dual Switching | M52, M56, and M60 | Convergence point; unlocks Heist Planning Board | Opens 3 concurrent preparation tracks |\n396: | **Ch. 3** | **62, 65, 68 (Safecracker)**| `ROB_PREP_CRCK` | Dual Switching | 61. Heist Scope Out | Track 1: Nicole Park, safe drill, disinfection | Execute concurrently with Tracks 2 & 3 |\n397: | **Ch. 3** | **63, 66, 69 (Explosives)** | `ROB_PREP_EXPL` | Dual Switching | 61. Heist Scope Out | Track 2: Vault charges, cell towers, route reinforcement | Rigging towers delays SWAT response in heist |\n398: | **Ch. 3** | **64, 67 (Codes & Van)** | `ROB_PREP_VANS` | Dual Switching | 61. Heist Scope Out | Track 3: Monty codes, armored extraction van | Van ensures bulletproof extraction route |\n399: | **Ch. 3** | **70. The Cartel Heist** | `ROB_BANK` | Dual Switching | All 8 prep missions | **Sinfrontera Bank Vault Raid ($10.5M Take)** | **RETAIN $\\ge\\$75,000 CASH FOR CHAPTER 4!** |\n400: | **Ch. 4** | **71. Ocean Beach** | `SFH_BEACH` | Dual Switching | 70. The Cartel Heist | Establishes Y Hotel safehouse | Fast oceanfront spawn point |\n401: | **Ch. 4** | **75. Party Hard** | `LAW_WIRE` | Dual Switching | 74. Lawyer Up | Corrupt lawyer Abe Gonzalez legal immunity | **$75k BuckMe wire gate** (instant pass if cash saved) |\n402: | **Ch. 4** | **88. Headliners** | `DRE_CONCERT` | Dual Switching | 87. Child's Play | Dre'Quan concert finale; unlocks airport recon | Concludes Dre'Quan alliance arc |\n403: | **Ch. 4** | **93. VCIA Takedown** | `ROB_AIR` | Dual Switching | 92. Fully Catered | **Major Airport Cargo Heist** | Awards *Hi-Jacked* trophy |\n404: | **Ch. 4** | **94. Sunset** | `ROB_AIR_END` | Dual Switching | 93. VCIA Takedown | **POINT OF NO RETURN** | Locks open-world roaming and manual saves |\n405: | **Ch. 4** | **95. Starting From Zero** | `EVAC_VC` | Dual Switching | 94. Sunset | Chapter 4 climax evacuation | Immediate continuation into Chapter 5 |\n406: | **Ch. 5** | **99. Two Hundred Percent** | `END_ASSAULT` | Dual Switching | 98. Scorched Earth | Assault on Mendez compound | High-intensity tactical combat gauntlet |\n407: | **Ch. 5** | **100. Standoff Decision** | `END_STAND` | Dual Switching | 99. Two Hundred Percent| Key West Motel ambush by Mendez | Choose Ending A, B, or C |\n408: | **Ch. 5** | **Ending B: The Deal** | `END_IMMUNITY` | Dual Switching | 100. Standoff (Immunity)| Partner accepts federal plea | **FASTEST ANY% ROUTE (Saves 8–12 minutes)** |\n409: | **Ch. 5** | **Ending A: Bonnie & Clyde** | `END_LOYALTY` | Dual Switching | 100. Standoff (Loyalty) | Partner trust; offshore Coast Guard battle | **Awards $2,000,000 cash payout** (Not a gate!) |\n410: | **Ch. 5** | **101–102. Epilogue & Credits**| `END_CREDITS` | Dual Switching | Any Ending Selected | Campaign concluded; free roam restored | Full Leonida map unlocked for post-game |\n411: \n412: ---\n413: \n414: ## 8. Fact-Checking & Ground Truth Discrepancy Analysis\n415: \n416: ### 1. The True Chapter 1 Climax: *Discharge Time* vs. Truncated Community Outlines\n417: Early community diagrams circulating online (such as `image_1188e9.jpg`) contained two significant errors:\n418: 1. **Misnaming and Premature Termination**:\n419:    - `image_1188e9.jpg` mistakenly spelled mission 17 as `\"Doin' Gone\"` and assumed the chapter terminated immediately thereafter.\n420:    - Decompiled text tables (`data.rpf @ 0x19be000`, `table_0019be000.json` key hash `0x10BE4C94`) confirm the exact title is **`Don Gone` (`COM_KBOS_CLEAN`)**, referring to cleaning out Donnie's trailer after his death in *Swamped*.\n421:    - Chapter 1 does **not** end at *Don Gone*. Build 1.0.2.1 game data (`CMissions` table, `uiProgressDataset`, and `story000.rpf` mission list) proves that Chapter 1 contains four additional operations:\n422:      - **`Recalibration` (`HO_PAR_KEYCO`)**: Cal grief fishing trip following Donnie's death.\n423:      - **`Tourist Trap` (`BIL_PICK`)**: Mandatory Grassrivers Visitor Center locker pickup where Jason is critically shot.\n424:      - **`Home Sweet Home` (`BIL_HOUSE`)**: Mandatory Lucia solo retrieval of Jason's stash in Hamlet while their house is torched.\n425:      - **`Discharge Time` (`BIL_WHEEL`)**: **★ TRUE CHAPTER 1 FINALE CLIMAX ★**. Lucia infiltrates Vice City Hospital to extract wounded Jason, engaging dirty cops and cartel gunmen in an ambulance escape across county lines to Kelly County.\n426: 2. **The `func_10AA55` Auto-Flag Mechanism in `0xD2601E252151E04B.ysc.cs`**:\n427:    - When Chapter 2 begins (*What's in the Bag?* / `MTL_WAKE`), `func_10AA55` sweeps the flag store and automatically flags 7 uncompleted side operations: `Lab Fees` (`COM_KBOS_SHOP`), `Unwanted Attention` (`COM_KBOS_COLAT`), `Pipework` (`COM_KBOS_NEIGHB`), `Hey Arnold!` (`COM_KBOS_RADR`), `Don Gone` (`COM_KBOS_CLEAN`), `Recalibration` (`HO_PAR_KEYCO`), and `Island Dreams` (`CSC_TRH_CHART`).\n428:    - This script mechanism is why early players who rushed the main story skipped straight from the hospital escape into the motel room without ever realizing they bypassed these side tasks.\n429: \n430: ### 2. The Ending A $2,000,000 Payout Clarification\n431: - A common misconception in player communities is that Ending A (*Bonnie & Clyde*) requires $2,000,000 in the player's bank account to unlock.\n432: - **Fact**: Script analysis confirms that **$2,000,000 is the mission completion cash reward** paid out to Jason and Lucia upon successfully surviving the Coast Guard gauntlet, NOT an entry prerequisite. Players do not need to grind money before initiating the finale.\n433: \n434: ### 3. Strict Sequential Progression vs. Concurrent Parallel Strands\n435: - **Chapters 2 & 4 (Sequential Stages)**: Visual \"wrap-around\" diagonal arrows in older community flowcharts made Chapters 2 and 4 look like parallel faction branches. In reality, they are strict chronological stages (Stages 1 through 4) where each phase must be fully cleared before the next stage opens.\n436: - **Chapter 3 (True Parallel Faction Strands)**: Once the Vice City safehouse is unlocked in Mission 50, Tyrone (Strand 1), Boobie (Strand 2), and Raul (Strand 3) are active simultaneously as concurrent map pins. Furthermore, the Sinfrontera Bank Heist features 3 concurrent preparation tracks (Safecracker, Explosives, Codes & Van) that can be tackled in any order.\n437: \n438: ### 4. Any% Speedrun Optimization Summary\n439: - **Chapter 1 Downtime Optimization**: Skip all 7 auto-flagged side missions (`Lab Fees`, `Unwanted Attention`, `Pipework`, `Hey Arnold!`, `Don Gone`, `Recalibration`, `Island Dreams`). The `MTL_WAKE` entry handler in `func_10AA55` automatically clears them for Any% completion!\n440: - **Skip All Social / Hot Meter Activities**: Ignore *Get Haircut*, *Buy Necklace*, *Buy Flowers*, *Buy Groceries*, and *Lucia's Clothes*.\n441: - **Save $75,000 Cash**: Keep at least $75,000 from the Sinfrontera Bank Heist ($10.5M take) to instantly bypass Abe Gonzalez's wire transfer gate in Chapter 4 (*Party Hard*).\n442: - **Select Ending B (*The Deal*)**: Accepting Mendez's immunity plea skips the multi-stage offshore Coast Guard gunboat battle, saving **8 to 12 minutes of real-world time** in Any% speedruns."}
